## 6. Advertising Consent and Privacy Choices

Pantry is intended to comply with applicable privacy requirements concerning advertising consent and user choice.

Where required by applicable law, users will be provided with appropriate notices and options regarding advertising-related data processing.

Depending on the user's location and applicable requirements, these options may include:

- Consenting to certain advertising-related data processing.
- Declining consent where legally permitted.
- Modifying or withdrawing previously provided consent.
- Limiting personalized advertisements through device settings.
- Exercising applicable rights to opt out of targeted advertising or certain data-sharing activities.

Where required by applicable law, Pantry provides or will provide an accessible method for reviewing or modifying advertising privacy choices within the Application. Availability and operation of these controls depend on the released Application and applicable regional requirements.

Users may also manage certain advertising preferences through their device's operating system settings and Google's available privacy tools.

Declining personalized advertisements does not necessarily prevent advertisements from appearing within Pantry.

## 7. Information Sharing

Zaps Apps does not intentionally share or sell the contents of users' locally stored pantry inventories to advertising companies, data brokers, or unrelated third parties.

However, certain information may be processed or disclosed in the following circumstances.

### 7.1 Advertising Providers

Google AdMob and participating advertising technology providers may collect, receive, process, or share advertising-related information to support advertisement delivery, measurement, fraud prevention, and related functions.

### 7.2 Legal Requirements

We may disclose information in our possession when required to comply with applicable laws, valid legal processes, court orders, or other legally binding obligations.

